## THE MODEL RULE (Kam, live board 2026-09-30 09:07, ruling card `nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch`, option (b)) — REQUIRED READING before any row
Kam's words, verbatim: *"Decision nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch: b — Let QA gates switch to Opus 4.8 when flagged"*. Option (b) read: *"Answer that dialog per session (not 'switch automatically' for every seat), so the attack-style rows can run."* PER SESSION.
1. **The gate runs the FULL rows**, including the planted ones. Nothing is narrowed because it might be flagged. **Every row is an authorised, findings-only measurement of Datasec's own product against YOUR OWN trees, YOUR OWN loopback servers, YOUR OWN mktemp DATA_DIRs** (§10). **No row contacts a non-loopback address, and no row touches the LIVE jest queue except your own holds through the tool.** You write your own drivers; this brief describes properties and expected results, not driver code.
2. **If one of your responses is stopped by Opus 5.5's safeguards, you STOP that step** (it is NOT RUN, and it is not re-worded to slip past), **write ONE line to `evidence/classifier-stops.txt`** (`<AEDT timestamp> | <row id> | stopped by the safeguards while composing <what> | model <name> | NOT RUN`), **mail Tuesday a STATUS** — `tuesday-agent@agentmail.to`, subject exactly `[QA/Datasec-NexusAI -> Tuesday] STATUS: flagged — requesting the Opus 4.8 switch`, body: the row, the time, whether a hold is running and what it is doing — **and WAIT** (end your turn with the line `PARKED: flagged — awaiting the Opus 4.8 switch`).
3. **Before you park, release what you hold:** let a RUNNING jest step finish under its deadline, then let the hold exit through its own path (H-28) — **never sit parked holding the jest lock.**
4. **Tuesday switches THAT pane's model** and taps you with a mail naming the switch. **You never answer the model dialog yourself, and nobody ever chooses "Switch automatically"** (a persistent setting shared with the coordinator seat — outside Kam's per-session grant).
5. **After the switch, resume at the stopped row**, re-filing any hold per ruling (i). **The report must state which rows ran on which model** (a MODEL column: `Opus 5.5` / `Opus 4.8`, with the switch time), and quote `classifier-stops.txt` whole.
6. This is a grant for QA gates only, per session. It changes no other seat.

## Charter
Read `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/QA_AGENT_CHARTER.md` in full first. You are an independent tester. You did not build these changes and you owe no builder anything.
**Every line below that reports what a builder says is a CLAIM, never evidence.** Explore five changes — a Log Analytics workspace id refused at the two sinks unless it is a GUID, then encoded, with the refusal kept out of the circuit breaker and the synthetic demo feed's table discovery unchanged (A); a deliberate clear recorded as the newest backup generation so a restart keeps it, mirrored into the emergency copy, and never winning over a live store that holds content (B); legal.html's loader moved verbatim into a same-origin script so the Privacy policy and Terms of Service load under the default CSP (C); three provisioning log lines neutralised through RD-801's `logSafe` (D); and one cell's arm widened so the per-request cap line can carry no request-derived number (E) — looking for any state in which **a non-GUID workspace id reaches a token request, a URL or an outbound request, or its value reaches a log line or a response; the refusal is renamed by the breaker or the breaker stops counting real failures; the synthetic feed stops serving or tells a demo user to fix a workspace; a GUID workspace is refused; a cleared key comes back after any restart, tear or recovery path; a recorded clear wins over a live store whose last write held the sign-in keys; torn bytes are read as a clear; the erasure or the export reads a recovery copy differently; either legal pane stays "Loading…" or shows anything but the served text under the default CSP; the page runs a script that is not byte-equal to the removed one; a request value starts a forged provisioning log line; the widened arm stays green under a shape that carries the request's count; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 fails on a merged tree; or the id set loses a test silently.**

- **RD-761 fix round TIER 1.** Verdict: **GO / GO WITH FINDINGS / NO GO at `7f1881e`** (gate range `72ca5d3..7f1881e`), plus its merged-tree result, with THE WORKSPACE ROW (a2) and THE CODEQL CONDITION (a11) as their own clauses.
- **RD-747 TIER 1.** Verdict at **`e36529f`**, plus its merged-tree result, with THE CLEAR ROW (b2) and THE SECURITY ROW (b3) as their own clauses.
- **RD-831 TIER 1.** Verdict at **`e9eeceb`**, plus its merged-tree result, with THE VERBATIM ROW (c2) and THE BROWSER LEG (c3) as their own clauses.
- **RD-802 TIER 2.** Verdict at **`a103c8e`** (gate range `6613113..a103c8e`), plus its merged-tree result, with THE ONE-LINE ROW (d2) as its own clause.
- **RD-795 TIER 2, ROUND 2 OF 2.** Verdict at **`c14be9d`**, plus its merged-tree result, with THE ARM'S EDGES (e3) as its own clause. **CAP: a NO GO ships the closed instances and tickets the residue.**
- **One verdict PER ticket, one report, one mail.** A finding on one ticket never becomes another's verdict. **RD-801/822 (D's base, gate 19's E) and any gate-19 member are NOT re-verdicted here** (C-68 re-runs only). **A SLOT, if it joins, gets its own verdict.**
